WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.530
Fireworks are blazing in the sky.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.370
Chaos is near.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.220
Which means...

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.530
What's needed is a hero!

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.370
It's been a long time since I had a relic...

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.920
The taste is so sweet,

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.420
so enchanting, so addictive!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.540
No way.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.420
This can't be...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.320
It sure is.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.740
I am the man of truth,

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.470
Doctor Ver!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.460
<b>Episode 10 
It's So Cruel, But...</b>

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.950
So you're using old LiNKER to merely

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.010
keep your Gears functional, huh?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.950
The only LiNKER made from 
kindness was what I made.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.180
They're making you fight with that?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.770
It's so pitiful, I can't stop laughing!

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.670
If anyone's pitiful here, it's you!

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.520
He stopped one of my hits...

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:02.780
<i>I'll repay the humiliation I suffered 
a million times over!</i>

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.110
Wait!

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.840
You can't hurt the doctor.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.040
What?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.960
But the only one who can make LiNKER is...

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.580
That's right.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.150
If something happens to me,

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.960
you'll lose LiNKER forever!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.130
He just showed up out of nowhere 
and won't stop talking.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.100
Even if you can't fight, I can!

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.590
It is unclear if he's friend or foe.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.860
Master, your orders.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.190
I'm not your friend or your enemy.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.360
I am a hero!

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.280
Then let's give you

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.210
an even bigger one!

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:49.120
<i>We're having a big sale on bullets.</i>

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.120
<i>And there's no cure for idiots.</i>

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.120
You birdbrain!

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.380
I don't know what you're thinking,

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.890
<i>Huge discounts on ass-kicking, 
now dance!</i>

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.560
but if you use that, both I and this facility

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.330
<i>It's time for a rodeo, baby!</i>

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.410
will be crushed by the seawater!

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.880
Just kidding.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.970
Leiur, get us out of this.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:07.470
<i>If you want to gripe at the world,</i>

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.390
Right away.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.460
<i>start being more than a mere target.</i>

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:17.110
<i>Gods and Buddhas, I'm through with you.</i>

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.690
<i>I can't let them handle this!</i>

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.680
<i>I'm their senpai!</i>

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:24.900
<i>Even if we've ripped off the scars and 
hidden the wounds (Trust Heart),</i>

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.590
You can't hit her like that.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:24.660
Calm down!

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.410
<i>can we help, and laugh at, one another—</i>

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.410
Do you plan to hit us, too?

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.920
Where did they go?

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.440
They must have gone down there.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.530
I let them go, huh?

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.790
I'm sorry.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.750
I thought that if something happened to the doctor, 
we couldn't make LiNKER anymore.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.140
But we won't be deceived again!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.590
If the three of us work together, this time—

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.370
I can't rely on your help!

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.280
We aren't dancing, hand-in-hand, 
through flower fields here.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.400
I'll do it myself.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.640
<i>I have to do it on my own,</i>

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.840
<i>or I can't call myself their senpai.</i>

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.560
Targets lost.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.170
Unless something big happens, 
I can't track them from here.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.180
Dr. Ver...

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.920
If they'd let us know he was stored there, 
this wouldn't have happened...

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.380
His Nephilim power is as strong as ever.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.710
This is a problem.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.300
Start trying to trace them again. Hurry.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.640
The destruction of the last part, 
the Yantra Sarvaswa,

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.910
means we've stopped the completion 
of the Château de Tiffauges.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.700
But Carol is still...

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.860
Please explain.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.960
The Château de Tiffauges I worked on

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.950
was meant to help us carry on our papa's will.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.660
You didn't say it would rip apart the world!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.730
Indeed.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.080
The Château de Tiffauges is a World Destructor,

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.920
the culmination of alchemical science,

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.940
and at the same time, a giant flask.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.920
You tricked me?

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.620
What will you do, now that you know?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.700
You have no power.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.560
Will you try to stop me?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.380
Even so...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:22.310
Even so, just how I love the 
papa beyond my memories,

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.940
I know you love him, too.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.430
What are you saying?

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:31.260
Papa doesn't want us to rip apart the world!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:34.530
I won't let you do something he doesn't want!

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.330
You're just a spare with replicated memories!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.840
You're a failure as his daughter, 
and you have no right to speak!

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.810
I'm releasing you from your duty 
to construct the Château.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.600
Go do whatever you want.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.850
Was I out?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.370
Another rejection.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.340
During our retreat, you lost consciousness.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.860
I can understand you being hasty when

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.220
multiple high-level phonic 
gainers are present, but...

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.770
There's no need to worry.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:12.890
I know you...

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.560
Dr. Ver, one of the parties involved 
in the Frontier Incident.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.040
What are you doing here?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.870
A bunch of selfish jerks who 
only care about themselves

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.800
decided to pretend that both my heroics and 
the Frontier Incident never happened!

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.790
I lost my rights and my very identity,

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.800
becoming a thing, not a person.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.460
I was thrown in there, as part of

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.300
the Nephilim they recovered.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.740
That left arm...

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:43.010
I didn't use the arm's power 
to block Ichaival's attack.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.440
At the moment of contact, 
Nephilim devoured, assimilated,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.250
and controlled its output, as part of its own body.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.620
You're an interesting man.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.030
Very well, follow me.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.000
You're going to take me out of here?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.190
Then lead me to the center of the chaos.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:01.580
The center of the chaos?

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.640
That's where a hero belongs.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.500
Nephilim's left arm...

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.670
Tell me more about its power

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:14.430
as we evade our pursuers.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:17.180
Don't you need to hurry and escape?

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:20.050
I know exactly where they are.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.530
It'll be easy to buy time.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.150
I'm not saying to not use your power!

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.020
I'm telling you to think about how you use it!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.550
Our new Symphogears exist

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.450
to fight Carol's alchemy!

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.660
This is precisely the way to use them.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.340
You're nuts, old man...

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:42.450
Don't forget that you're at the bottom of the sea!

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.290
You can't fight the supernatural 
with common sense!

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:51.110
Just in case, check the bulkheads

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.880
and purge switches for all blocks.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.900
I... I can't remember all these.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.920
Then, Kiri-chan, let's each remember half.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.810
I've found traces of an intruder 
in the security system.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.560
That's what I've been waiting to hear!

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.320
This is that...

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.390
Yes.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.610
The remains of the Autoscorer 
that Tsubasa-san defeated.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.330
It's still functional in this state?

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.650
I'm sorry for insulting...

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.630
your song.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.450
It was truly

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:34.170
a splendid song, sword girl.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.880
My song?

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.180
It was such a wonderfully cursed melody,

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.060
it felt like my body was being ripped in half!

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.370
A cursed melody...

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.760
Carol said the same thing before.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.990
You're going to answer us!

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:58.880
How far do we have to go?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.990
We should have caught up by now...

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.740
Are you sure this is the right way?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:04.880
Yeah.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.750
But they're doing a very good job of evading us.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.180
It's like they know our location and 
what routes we're choosing.

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:18.010
No way. They hacked our HQ?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.180
They slipped us poison without our knowledge?

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:27.270
Sorry to call you so late.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.730
I was thinking about stuff, and I couldn't sleep.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.770
No, don't worry about it.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.110
Thank you.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.310
After talking to you,

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:40.300
I've decided to talk to Dad once more.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:41.390
Yeah.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.210
But to be honest,

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:45.890
I'm still a little scared.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.490
I'm just so worried about what will happen.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.960
Hibiki, it's okay. Everything's just fine.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.740
That's what you always say.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:58.660
I forget when I started saying it...

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:03.250
They're magic words to make you feel 
it will work out, no matter what.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.090
You really are so simple.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.560
I prefer the term "optimistic."

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:14.510
That was a good laugh.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.730
You're sounding better.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.950
You should thank your magic words.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.580
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:25.450
You were slipped poison without knowing,

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.950
and when you find out, it will be too late.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.210
Certain death awaits.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:36.210
The fact that they can dodge 
our pursuit so easily...

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.210
And that they located the relics' location...

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.220
They've been peeking at our information?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.750
If that's the poison we've been slipped,

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.190
there's someone on the inside.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.640
N-No! I didn't do anything!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.160
It isn't me!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:54.610
No, it is you, Elfnein.

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.110
What is this?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.610
H-How?

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.070
Carol...

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.780
No way.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.320
I'm the poison?

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.920
What do you mean by "poison"?

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.380
There were several things my master needed

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:19.380
to dissect the world.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.340
One of them is the

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.890
magic sword's cursed melody.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.400
The Autoscorers' task was to make the wielders

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:32.640
sing the magic sword's cursed melody, 
and carve it into our bodies for recovery.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.270
Then the Ignite Module...

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:38.650
Impossible! I refuse to suspect Elfnein!

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.640
But Elfnein had no way

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:45.360
of knowing she was the poison.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:49.070
I've been jacking her eyes, ears,

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:52.910
and all other senses.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:56.320
My senses were being controlled?

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:01.920
I could do it because she's a homunculus, 
created from the same template as myself.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.960
When my master was, herself,

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:09.010
hit with the cursed melody, the score was created.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.520
The only thing left was the easy part,

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:15.060
making you use the Ignite Modules.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.560
Then it was all planned from the start?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.890
Please... Please tie me up!

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:27.570
Throw me in a prison, so I can't see anyone.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.640
No, my task of telling you Carol's plans

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:34.320
is already complete.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.080
So you can just...

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.180
Then, now that she has the cursed melodies,

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:47.340
there's no reason to let the wielders live?

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.760
That's why she focused on distracting us?

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.180
Ogawa-san! Contact HQ!

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.850
We need to tell them not to 
use the Ignite Modules!

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.540
It's no good. This is probably chaff.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.190
They've blocked the whole area's communications.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:04.650
Clever!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.950
So... So...

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.160
So just...

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.260
I'm glad, then...

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.210
That you aren't a bad girl.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.960
You were just being used by the enemy.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.440
Tomosato-san? Fujitaka-san?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.830
Your goal is to stop Carol's plans.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.720
See it to the end.

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.560
Genjuurou-san...

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.150
So stay here.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:40.230
We don't care who's watching us.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.270
O-Okay.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.470
She's just a tool. How dare she?

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.720
This is the end... Carol! Doctor!

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.120
It won't be as easy as last time.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.060
I've already found a replacement for the final part

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.770
I need to complete the Château.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:10.580
I wouldn't mind being a hero kids love,

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.850
but I'm a little busy!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.010
Who would ever love you?

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:25.820
<i>Zeios Igalima raizen tron.</i>

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.100
<i>Danger signals flashing.</i>

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.220
<i>Hell or Heaven, which do ya want? Death!</i>

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:03.320
Engagement start.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.110
Putting full energy into combat control.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:08.410
<i>Attention! If you want to get chopped in half...</i>

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.940
Type Alpha 100 Samsara

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.320
<i>Watch out! Death!</i>

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:13.430
<i>A past you're a bit ashamed of,</i>

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.140
<i>burned aware in a blushing flare! Death!</i>

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.240
<i>How high do I have to stack 'em</i>

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.100
<i>before I can see the future?</i>

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:28.230
<i>These rails just go forward, right? Death!</i>

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:31.700
<i>Let's kiss and dream of a world</i>

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.700
My sister and I...

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.340
<i>that we'll never cut apart!</i>

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.340
will handle this... once she arrives.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:40.860
<i>If you just keep looking for what 
it takes to be stronger,</i>

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:37.010
Your task as an Autoscorer...

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:38.760
I shall be flashy when I complete it.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:46.480
<i>you'll never fulfill your true desires.</i>

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:43.270
Bye-bye!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.480
Wait!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.330
<i>Holding the courage to be strong in your heart...</i>

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.190
This is bad!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.530
You can't get close because you 
can't use your full firepower!

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.660
No, the flow is getting thrown off.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:08.630
Guys!

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:31.490
Someone who's alone shouldn't want friends,

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:35.020
or comrades, or to be a senpai...

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.990
Otherwise... Otherwise...

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.580
This cruel world will kill them all,

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.000
and you'll really be alone!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.210
Why did Mom and Dad try to save 
this world with their songs,

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.790
when it's so cruel?

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.970
If you have time to cry, then sing!

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:03.950
You aren't alone.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:07.670
We may not be good for much.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:12.270
But we can stay by your side, 
so you aren't alone.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:17.660
Guys...

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:21.680
It was a bit of a shock to hear that

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.330
you didn't want to be our senpai.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.490
We rely...

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:28.410
on you to be...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.430
our senpai!

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.320
I see.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:38.430
If even someone like me can be your senpai,

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.810
then I can have friends like you!

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:46.140
I'm not scared anymore.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.150
<i>Ignite Module! Drawn Blade!</i>

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:52.890
<i>Dáinsleif.</i>

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:03.740
They're counting on me

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.910
to be their senpai.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.660
I have to live up to that...

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.020
Even if someone else

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:13.920
could let that happen, I can't!

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.280
<i>I was about to give up</i>

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:40.360
<i>all the strength and warmth I'd finally found</i>

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.910
<i>because I was so scared of losing it.</i>

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.540
She's using her rifle...

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.710
To hit you!

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:57.150
<i>This world gave me</i>

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:58.880
<i>my bonds with them.</i>

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:01.640
<i>It takes away what you care about,</i>

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.720
<i>but sometimes, it gives you 
something else to care for.</i>

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.140
<i>So that's it.</i>

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:09.160
<i>Mom and Dad used their songs to bring peace,</i>

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.020
<i>so that the world would have more to care for...</i>

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.400
Is she planning to kill everyone here?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:34.000
I remember where the switch is!

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.580
We did it!

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:50.190
We devised that combination on the spot.

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:52.560
That was madness...

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.380
It was only possible

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:57.060
because you guys were here.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:01.070
Thanks.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.840
The Undersea Dragon Palace is badly damaged.

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:13.460
It's begun collapsing near their location.

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:17.360
A massive object is approaching at high speed.

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:18.710
It's...

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:22.090
That humanoid weapon?

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.010
Are the wielders out?

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.760
It's no good. We won't make it...

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:33.270
Was our combination useless?

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.270
Don't give up yet!

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:46.910
They've arrived at the sub.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:48.380
Surface immediately!

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.660
Forget about depressurization! 
Just get away from it!

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:58.420
Get all crew to the bridge, 
and brace for impact!

00:21:58.760 --> 00:21:59.970
Hurry, Tomosato!

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:07.080
The morning of the final battle...
